{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfenKLCARsponLH4HrZ7U","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written all three files for the candidate, and the self-check prints `OK`. It didn't check novelty against the other models, and it couldn't check convergence: the smoke fit used one chain, so there is no R-hat, and admission's full fit still has to show R-hat ≤ 1.05 and bulk ESS ≥ 100.\n\n**Which model and what changed:** I refined `personal_lapse_ideal_streak_excess`, which is 1.9× dse behind the incumbent, so statistically tied with it. It keeps its mechanism: each person's own ideal switching rate, a penalty for every flip of the longest streak beyond two, and each person's own lapse rate. The one change is a shared bias toward the sequence with the larger share of heads, applied when the person is evaluating rather than lapsing. The idea is that heads is the outcome people expect from a coin, so a heads-heavy sequence looks more like real coin flipping.\n\n**Why this change:** it targets the critique's strongest result that survives the FDR, `heads_majority_pref` (q = 0.032). Among pairs with equal switch counts, people chose the heads-heavier sequence 0.567 of the time, against 0.425 for the incumbent's simulated data. The incumbent treats heads and tails the same, so it can't produce that. The base model's streak penalty already covers the critique's other result, the preference for the sequence with the shorter longest run.\n\n**Self-check results:**\n- **Smoke fit:** 100 tuning and 100 draws on one chain, 60 seconds of sampling.\n- **ELPD-LOO:** -1071.1. That is about 3.6 nats better than the base model's -1067.5 would need to be to match it, so on this short fit it is roughly level with the base model, not ahead. A short fit can't settle that.\n- **PSIS-LOO reliability:** 162 of 2560 trials (6.3%) have Pareto k > 0.5, above the 1% tolerance, so the check flagged the estimate as unreliable. If the full fit gives the same verdict, the model can't be the exported winner, which has to be the best model with a reliable PSIS-LOO.\n\nThe model name is `heads_favoring_lapse_ideal_streak`. Files are in `/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_4/candidate_5/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3224,"cache_read_input_tokens":66850,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3224,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":721,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e459668-56b2-463e-b858-c7aa0999d650","uuid":"6bbda1af-0e66-42a9-85b8-f308d4e8fbe1","timestamp":"2026-10-03T05:51:48.366Z","request_id":"req_011CfenKKocAyKJF1TMfVey6"}
